#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:663
msgid "Comma/Tab/Semicolon Separated Value (CSV/TSV) File Formats"
msgstr "Filformat för kommaseparerade eller tabbseparerade värden (CSV/TSV)"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:667
msgid ""
"The Comma Separated Value (CSV) and Tab Separated Value (TSV) file formats "
"are a common structuring strategy for text format files. In these files, "
"each line in the file represents a row of data and, within each line of the "
"file, the different data fields are separated from one another using a "
"separator character, often a comma, semicolon or tab. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> handles CSV and TSV files through the "
"text importer and exporter but these formats are given their own definitions"
" in this document because they are considered very common formats."
msgstr ""
"Filformaten CSV (kommaseparerade värden) och TSV (tabbseparerade värden) är "
"vanliga sätt att strukturera textfiler. Varje rad motsvarar en datarad, och "
"fälten i raden skiljs åt med ett avgränsningstecken, oftast kommatecken, "
"semikolon eller tabulatortecken. <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"hanterar CSV- och TSV-filer med textimportören och textexportören. Formaten "
"beskrivs ändå separat här eftersom de är så vanliga."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:680
msgid ""
"<application>Gnumeric</application> will automatically open CSV and TSV "
"format files separating each row into columns based on the presence of "
"appropriate separator characters in the file. If the automatic import leads "
"to any errors, these can generally be corrected by using the \"Text Import "
"(configurable)\" file format instead. Selecting that file format will launch"
" the <interface>Text Import</interface> druid which allows the user to "
"import CSV and TSV format files while specifying in greater detail the "
"settings of the import configuration parameters. See the section on <link "
"linkend=\"sect-file-textImport\">importing text files</link> or the section "
"on <link linkend=\"sect-file-textExport\">exporting text files</link> for an"
" explanation of how to open or save CSV and TSV files through the "
"<interface>Text Import</interface> druid."
msgstr ""
"<application>Gnumeric</application> öppnar CSV- och TSV-filer automatiskt "
"och delar upp varje rad i kolumner utifrån avgränsningstecknen. Om importen "
"ger fel kan de oftast rättas genom att välja filformatet ”Textimport "
"(konfigurerbar)” i stället. Då öppnas guiden "
"<interface>Textimport</interface>, där du kan ange fler importinställningar "
"för CSV- och TSV-filer. Avsnitten om <link linkend=\"sect-file-"
"textImport\">import av textfiler</link> och <link linkend=\"sect-file-"
"textExport\">export av textfiler</link> beskriver hur du öppnar och sparar "
"CSV- och TSV-filer med guiden <interface>Textimport</interface>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:704
msgid "Comma/Semicolon/Tab Separated Value, CSV/TSV"
msgstr ""
"Kommaseparerade, semikolonseparerade och tabbseparerade värden (CSV/TSV)"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:716
msgid "Many"
msgstr "Många"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:735
msgid ""
"The CSV file format is only useful for the exchange of cell data and cannot "
"be used for sheet objects like graphical plots. This file format cannot save"
" the formatting of cell contents, backgrounds or borders."
msgstr ""
"CSV-formatet lämpar sig bara för att utbyta celldata. Det kan inte användas "
"för bladobjekt som diagram och kan inte spara cellinnehållens formatering, "
"bakgrunder eller kantlinjer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:749 C/gnumeric.xml:3118
msgid "Supported by the core <application>Gnumeric</application> program."
msgstr "Stöds av <application>Gnumeric</application>-kärnan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:760
msgid ""
"CSV files are simple text files where each row of the text file represents "
"one row in the spreadsheet and where the cells within a row are separated "
"from each other by a comma."
msgstr ""
"CSV-filer är enkla textfiler där varje rad motsvarar en rad i kalkylbladet "
"och cellerna skiljs åt med kommatecken."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:774
msgid ""
"CSV files can be processed using any tool which operates on text files. The "
"CSV format is also common as a format which can be opened by applications."
msgstr ""
"Du kan bearbeta CSV-filer med alla verktyg som hanterar textfiler. Formatet "
"är också vanligt bland program som kan öppna filer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:784
msgid ""
"<emphasis role=\"italic\">See the section on </emphasis> <link "
"linkend=\"file-format-text\">Text Formats</link>"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis role=\"italic\">Se avsnittet om </emphasis> <link linkend=\"file-"
"format-text\">textformat</link>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:801
msgid "Data Interchange Format (DIF) File Format"
msgstr "Filformatet Data Interchange Format (DIF)"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:803
msgid ""
"The Data Interchange Format (DIF) file format is a text based format encoded"
" in ASCII with a header, for integrity checking, and a body. The format was "
"originally developed by Software Arts in order to transfer data from "
"<application>VisiCalc</application>, the first spreadsheet."
msgstr ""
"Data Interchange Format (DIF) är ett textbaserat ASCII-format med ett huvud "
"för integritetskontroll och en brödtext. Software Arts tog ursprungligen "
"fram formatet för att överföra data från "
"<application>VisiCalc</application>, det första kalkylprogrammet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:818
msgid "Data Interchange Format"
msgstr "Datautbytesformat"

